			}]
			title: "Into the Twilight"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["67BC6ABF61224134"]
			description: [
				"The &aNaga&r guards the first hollow hill. Kill it to begin the Twilight Forest progression - the book unlocks the next boss."
				""
				"&e&lThe Naga is the doorway to the rest of the Twilight.&r Killing it unlocks the next hollow hill, and the chain of bosses that follows ends in trophies you need for the Celestial Core."
				""
				"&e&lThe fight:&r a spiral courtyard with a segmented serpent that charges in straight lines and smashes the pillars. It cannot be outrun."
				"&7- &fUse the pillars.&7 Break its charge by putting stone between you. It destroys them, which is fine - there are plenty."
				"&7- &fHit the head&7, not the body segments."
				"&7- &fIt alternates&7 between charging and a slower circling phase. Attack during the circle, hide during the charge."
				"&7- &fBring a shield&7 and food. This is a stamina fight, not a burst fight."
				""
				"&e&lDrops:&r &7Naga Scales&r (a full armour set) plus the &7Naga Trophy&r - one of the five you will need for the Celestial Core. &lKeep the trophy.&r"
				""
				"&8Iron gear is enough if you use the terrain. Diamond makes it comfortable. Do not bring your only good sword and no backup."
			]
			icon: "twilightforest:naga_trophy"
			id: "321DE9424210F3F1"
			rewards: [{
				count: 9
				id: "51A7A36D2BE9D256"
				item: "twilightforest:naga_scale"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Scale armour and the first trophy"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "twilightforest:naga"
				id: "0481725F962E0ED5"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "The Naga"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["321DE9424210F3F1"]
			description: [
				"The &5Lich&r in his tower is the gatekeeper of the whole dimension. Beat him and the deeper biomes stop hurting you."
				""
				"&c&lHe is a hard progression lock, not an optional boss.&r Until the Lich dies the Twilight Forest actively punishes you for entering its deeper biomes - you take escalating damage and simply cannot proceed. Everything past this point in the chapter needs him dead first."
				""
				"&e&lThe fight has three distinct phases:&r"
				"&71.&r &7Shield phase&7 - he floats behind orbiting shields and fires homing bolts. &lReflect them back with a sword&r; each reflected bolt breaks one shield. Melee is useless here."
				"&72.&r &7Summon phase&7 - shields down, he teleports and spawns zombies and skeletons. Clear adds, chase him down."
				"&73.&r &7Melee phase&7 - out of tricks, he fights directly. This part is short."
				""
				"&7A shield helps enormously in phase one. Do not waste arrows on him while the shields are up.&r"
				""
				"&e&lDrops:&r scepters (the Twilight and Zombie scepters are genuinely useful) and the &7Lich Trophy&r - Celestial Core component number two. &lKeep the trophy.&r"
				""
				"&8The tower is full of lesser liches on the lower floors. Clear them first so nothing interrupts the real fight."
			]
			icon: "twilightforest:lich_trophy"
			id: "7194AE474BDDA510"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7D6E4A4E7E1C768C"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "twilightforest:lifedrain_scepter"
					tag: {
						Damage: 0
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Trophy for the Celestial Core"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "twilightforest:lich"
				id: "219FACD6690D1306"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "The Lich"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7194AE474BDDA510"]
			description: [
				"The &cHydra&r of the Fire Swamp: three heads, a lot of fire. Its blood forges some of the best gear in the realm."
				""
				"&c&lThis fight pays for wireless AE2.&r Fiery Blood smelts into &7Fiery Ingots&r, and Fiery Ingots are the frame of the &bQuantum Ring&r - the block that links your island network to the Moon, Mars and everywhere else. It also forges &7Fission Reactor Casings&r, so Ascension runs through here too."
				""
				"&e&lThe fight:&r three heads that attack independently, breathe fire, and bite. Heads you destroy grow back unless you are fast."
				"&7- &fFire resistance is close to mandatory.&7 Potion, or Fiery armour if you already have some."
				"&7- &fKill heads quickly&7 - damaged heads regenerate if you take too long between them."
				"&7- &fStay under it&7 where the fire breath cannot easily track you."
				"&7- &fBring a bow&7 for the heads you cannot safely reach."
				"&7- &fBlock up the swamp approach&7 - the surrounding area is hostile and you do not want adds mid-fight."
				""
				"&e&lDrops:&r &7Fiery Blood&r (smelt for Fiery Ingots) and the &7Hydra Trophy&r - Celestial Core component number three. &lKeep the trophy.&r"
				""
				"&8Do not attempt this in iron. This is the first Twilight boss that genuinely expects enchanted diamond or better."
			]
			icon: "twilightforest:hydra_trophy"
			id: "10583B7DED57F345"
			rewards: [
